00:05:44.420 --> 00:05:47.990
Is it possible to connect to
the public IP of a Cloud SQL

00:05:47.990 --> 00:05:50.450
instance from a private
Cloud Run service?

00:05:50.450 --> 00:05:53.230
Ooh, I've been asked this one
before when visiting customers.

00:05:53.230 --> 00:05:56.900
Also is this
cross-project set up?

00:05:56.900 --> 00:05:58.850
Cloud Run service and
Cloud SQL instance

00:05:58.850 --> 00:06:00.560
are on separate GCP
projects, so can you

00:06:00.560 --> 00:06:02.480
do a cross-project
setup with your database

00:06:02.480 --> 00:06:04.272
and you're running a
server somewhere else?

00:06:04.272 --> 00:06:05.000
Priyanka?

00:06:05.000 --> 00:06:06.500
PRIYANKA VERGADIA:
You actually can.

00:06:06.500 --> 00:06:08.000
So you have-- so
in this scenario,

00:06:08.000 --> 00:06:11.630
you have a Cloud SQL
instance in one project,

00:06:11.630 --> 00:06:16.070
and you have your
compute or whatever

00:06:16.070 --> 00:06:19.610
is calling that Cloud SQL
instance in another project.

00:06:19.610 --> 00:06:21.830
And you could totally
make them work

00:06:21.830 --> 00:06:28.490
by using what is called
as private service access.

00:06:28.490 --> 00:06:32.060
What it does is it connects
the two together even

00:06:32.060 --> 00:06:33.470
with a private IP.

00:06:33.470 --> 00:06:37.760
So you don't even have to expose
a public IP for your Cloud SQL

00:06:37.760 --> 00:06:40.760
instance, which again comes
back to the security point

00:06:40.760 --> 00:06:42.050
you were making earlier--

00:06:42.050 --> 00:06:43.820
everybody has to
think about security.

00:06:43.820 --> 00:06:46.010
So you're not exposing
with public IP.

00:06:46.010 --> 00:06:49.250
You're just using the private
IP of your Cloud SQL instance,

00:06:49.250 --> 00:06:51.950
and connecting it to
the virtual machine

00:06:51.950 --> 00:06:55.640
or wherever you're
running your compute

00:06:55.640 --> 00:06:56.930
to call your servers from.

00:06:56.930 --> 00:06:57.830
So it's possible.

00:06:57.830 --> 00:06:59.868
Private service
access is the service

00:06:59.868 --> 00:07:02.160
you're looking for to kind
of connect the two together.

00:07:02.160 --> 00:07:03.303
It's a VPC offering.

00:07:03.303 --> 00:07:04.220
AJA HAMMERLY: Awesome.

00:07:04.220 --> 00:07:05.700
Thank you so much, Priyanka.

00:07:05.700 --> 00:07:06.200
